Another reason not to play Moria...  :-)

>So being blind and telepathic
>would be like an at-will detect monsters spell, but not worth much more.
>It would also eliminate the effective immunity from yellow lights that
>you get once you eat a floating eye.

Admittedly, yellow lights are pretty dangerous unless you have telepathy, and
pretty trivial otherwise. But bear in mind that the creation of a yellow light
dilutes your chances of getting something more killable, edible, 
treasure-leaving... They have their place, even after gaining telepathy.

>     Oh, one last note: "You can't see in here!" when engulfed by a vortex.
>What the *hell* does this mean?... 

With the exception of air elementals, all vortices have some sort of blocking,
blinding or distorting properties which counteract normal sight. And IMHO no
exception should be made for air elementals, either, since the player is going
to be whirled around so quickly that vision would be no better than a blur.
Maybe the message should be changed in this case, though...

